How to connect volume to an linux instance 

Create an linux instance and connect it with putty 

Now take a look at the disk sections by using this command
	"df -h" [disk free human readable]
	
After that give this command "lsblk" list block to see the unmounted volume in the instance.

Now we're going to make a file system and directory to mount the extra volume

These are the commands to make a file system and directory

	Mkfs -t ext4 <path of  unmounted volume>
	
	Make files system 
	-t = type of the file
	Ext4 = format of the file
	
	Mkdir /<directory name>
	
After that we're going to mount the volume

	Mount <file system path> <directory path>
	
	Mount /dev/xvdc  /usoop

We can also modify the volume like we did in the windows system

Change the volume size and enter this command

	"resize2fs  /dev/xvdc  /usoop"
	
	

